WEBVTT

NOTE Narration transcribed from the subtitles burned into fig-journey.mp4; timings read at 0.5 s resolution.

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.500
A fully ripe fig is one of
the most fragile fruits on earth.

2
00:00:03.500 --> 00:00:08.000
…yet somehow, these delicate fruits travel
from the rugged Aegean mountains

3
00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:11.500
to premium international tables
without turning to mush.

4
00:00:11.500 --> 00:00:12.000
How?

5
00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:17.000
It requires an unbroken chain of
traditional care and modern logistics.

6
00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:20.500
The journey begins at the source,
where growers of the Turkish Sarılop fig

7
00:00:20.500 --> 00:00:26.500
wait for exact signs of ripeness… tiny skin
cracks, and a single drop of nectar at the base.

8
00:00:26.500 --> 00:00:32.500
Because the structure is so delicate, every piece
is hand-picked at dawn before the midday heat softens the skin.

9
00:00:32.500 --> 00:00:36.500
The fresh figs are then laid out on
traditional raised wooden mesh frames.

10
00:00:36.500 --> 00:00:40.000
Instead of artificial ovens,
the dry north winds and sun naturally

11
00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:43.000
concentrate the sugars
into a thick caramel texture.

12
00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:47.500
Once fully sun-cured, the dried fruit
faces a strict field inspection.

13
00:00:47.500 --> 00:00:51.000
Every single fig is manually checked
for softness and flesh thickness.

14
00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:53.000
Only the highest grades survive.

15
00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:57.500
The approved harvest is loaded into aerated crates
and securely transported down the mountain…

16
00:00:57.500 --> 00:01:02.000
…straight into a state-of-the-art processing facility
to meet rigorous global safety standards.

17
00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:06.500
Delivering this fragile regional fruit
to a global market requires a perfect sequence…

18
00:01:06.500 --> 00:01:11.500
…ancient, climate-driven patience in the field,
and hyper-modern hygiene at the finish line.
